<section class="faq-section" id="faqs">
  <div class="faq-inner">
    <div class="faq-heading">
      <span class="faq-eyebrow">TECHNICAL FIT</span>

      <h2>
        Common questions <br />
        <span>before scope is fixed.</span>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-number">01</span>

          <span class="faq-question">Where does Axys3D fit in an AEC delivery team?</span>

          <span class="faq-plus">+</span>
        </summary>

        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Axys3D adds governed production capacity across BIM, Revit, coordination support and
            visual outputs. Client-appointed professionals retain design authority, compliance
            decisions and statutory sign-off.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-number">02</span>

          <span class="faq-question">
            Can one engagement combine BIM and visualization outputs?
          </span>

          <span class="faq-plus">+</span>
        </summary>

        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Yes, when the authoritative inputs, intended uses, review owners and information-freeze
            points are defined. Each downstream output keeps its own approval and handoff
            requirements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-number">03</span>

          <span class="faq-question">How is confidential project information handled?</span>

          <span class="faq-plus">+</span>
        </summary>

        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Work defaults to private. Project identity, media, outcomes and credits require explicit
            publication approval. NDA, withdrawn and review-expired records remain outside public
            builds.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span class="faq-number">04</span>

          <span class="faq-question">What is needed to scope a first production package?</span>

          <span class="faq-plus">+</span>
        </summary>

        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            A useful starting brief names the project stage, source files, standards, disciplines,
            intended deliverables, review milestones, approval owners and required handoff formats.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
